Patch summary:
Looking up a Vulkan handle no longer takes a mutex once more than 16000 are
alive. The boxed handle table keeps its first handles in an array read
without a lock and every handle past that in a map behind one mutex, which
each lookup of such a handle took: every decoded command looks up its
command buffer, so the threads decoding and recording for a guest queued on
that mutex. The array now holds 65536 handles (4 MB), and the map past it is
read under a read-write lock, which lookups share.
